{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>On the third month.</b> We do not know the reason for 'on this day' unless the interpretation of R. Moses [ibn Giyyat] is correct, namely that it is the new moon, like 'tomorrow is the new moon' (1 Samuel 20:18). And Scripture mentions this because a few days after the day of their encamping the giving of the Torah took place. Perhaps on one day he went up to HaShem and came down and spoke with Israel, and on the third day of the month he went up another time to relay the people's words to HaShem, and there he was told that on the third day the giving of the Torah would be. And all this is by way of reasoning, for we rely on tradition that the Torah was given on the sixth of Sivan. And according to the intercalation, it was the sixth day of the week, if the month of Iyyar was not intercalated. Perhaps the reason for 'on this day' is that the distance between Rephidim and Mount Sinai was greater than the distance of any journey:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Resolved ר' משה as R. Moses ibn Giyyat, the most likely referent among Ibn Ezra's contemporaries named Moses consulted by name. The final clause is rendered hyper-literally; the comparison is elliptical and the sentence breaks off without a main verb."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:48.670558750Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}